# The `_astro` directory starts with an underscore, which Jekyll (GitHub
# Pages' default build engine) would skip entirely. An empty `.nojekyll`
# file in the build output tells GitHub to serve the files as-is.
#
# This file lives in `public/`, and Astro copies everything in `public/`
# to the root of the build output — so it lands in `dist/.nojekyll`
# automatically, no extra build step needed.
